WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.701 --> 00:00:03.100
♪♪

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.100
-I want to start
by addressing all of you

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.501
who recommended
I start using a coaster

00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:10.133
when I have a drink at my desk.

00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:12.367
I appreciate the advice.

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:18.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:23.300
We showed a picture
of a stand-up flyer of mine,

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.434
and someone said,
"That is a bad flyer

00:00:26.434 --> 00:00:30.501
because there is
no date, time, or place."

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:36.834
Well, I guess that explains
why it was so poorly attended.

00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:38.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.801 --> 00:00:46.033
A cowboy's rope
is called a lariat.

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:49.033
Lasso is what you do with it.

00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:51.634
"There's no faster way
to reveal yourself as a layman

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:55.701
to a cowboy
than by calling it a lasso."

00:00:55.701 --> 00:00:59.601
The second-fastest way
to reveal yourself as a layman

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:02.200
is every time a male horse pees,

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:04.367
you say, "Oh, my God!"

00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:06.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:17.067
Once a pumpkin is carved,
it is no longer a pumpkin.

00:01:17.067 --> 00:01:18.501
It's a Jack-o'-lantern.

00:01:18.501 --> 00:01:19.767
Fine.

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:26.434
Um, an ornithologist wrote in.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.868 --> 00:01:33.300
Said, "There's no such thing
as a seagull.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:36.501
They're called herring gulls."

00:01:36.501 --> 00:01:37.634
Hmm.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.601
That's not what I'm "herring."

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:53.634
Trump's plane is a 757,
not a 747.

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:55.901
However...

00:01:55.901 --> 00:01:59.367
when Trump's doctor
gave the plane a physical,

00:01:59.367 --> 00:02:01.267
he said it was a 215.

00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:07.400
Topical.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.267
I read the research.

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:15.801
We talked about the artist T.J.

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:20.133
who drew the photo
of Scollins in a tank top

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:23.467
and then wore it to the show
on a tank top.

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:28.634
And someone said he looks like
an unkempt Hunter Biden.

00:02:30.934 --> 00:02:34.167
To which I'll say, since when
is Hunter Biden kempt?

00:02:34.167 --> 00:02:35.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.934 --> 00:02:43.033
Had a joke about a Ford Escort.

00:02:43.033 --> 00:02:46.434
Multiple people wrote in
to say the Ford Escort we showed

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:49.267
was the European Ford Escort

00:02:49.267 --> 00:02:53.567
that was never available
in the States.

00:02:53.567 --> 00:02:56.801
You all said it was
a better Ford Escort, but...

00:02:56.801 --> 00:03:00.868
Did not work with our joke
about a county fair.

00:03:00.868 --> 00:03:05.601
Long story short, we have
a foreign exchange student

00:03:05.601 --> 00:03:07.334
in the graphics department.

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:10.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.834 --> 00:03:14.000
Not my favorite.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.234
And I'll go down and be like,

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:16.734
"Hey, just in the future,
use the Ameri..."

00:03:16.734 --> 00:03:21.033
He's like -- [French accent]
"But there was one, yeah?

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:22.767
There was also
a European Ford Escort.

00:03:22.767 --> 00:03:25.300
It was better."

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.634
And I'm like,
"Francois, just..."

00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:28.300
He's like, "Yeah,
well, maybe you could have

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:31.200
Sal choose a car that did not
have a European..."

00:03:33.934 --> 00:03:37.400
"If you leave it up to me,
I'm gonna choose the best."

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:38.934
Very quiet.

00:03:38.934 --> 00:03:40.701
[ Laughter ]
"Ohh..."

00:03:42.834 --> 00:03:48.601
We made a joke about
Kyrgyzstan needing more vowels.

00:03:48.601 --> 00:03:51.234
Someone wrote in and said,
"Kyrgyzstan has three vowels

00:03:51.234 --> 00:03:53.400
and seven consonants,
which is pretty balanced.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:57.901
The two Y's are both vowels."

00:03:57.901 --> 00:04:01.200
I will respond
to this Kyrgyzstan correction

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:04.400
with a famous quote
from neighboring Kazakhstan.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:06.501
[as Borat] "My wife."

00:04:06.501 --> 00:04:08.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.634 --> 00:04:18.400
We said a 17-year-old
carnival worker --

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.467
A 17-year-old carnival worker.

00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:24.868
A bunch of you said
this dude's not 17.

00:04:24.868 --> 00:04:27.934
All I'll say is the
carnival life is unforgiving.

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:29.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:34.634
You know how many times
this guy's watched

00:04:34.634 --> 00:04:38.734
a kid barf up a funnel cake?

00:04:38.734 --> 00:04:40.667
It'll age ya!

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:46.234
We talked about a county fair

00:04:46.234 --> 00:04:49.734
and sort of one of those
dangerous roller coasters.

00:04:49.734 --> 00:04:53.367
And I said in the wheel well,

00:04:53.367 --> 00:04:55.100
rattling around
in the wheel well,

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:58.601
you saw an ankle bone.

00:04:58.601 --> 00:05:00.801
Bunch of you said
there's no such thing

00:05:00.801 --> 00:05:03.267
as a human ankle bone.

00:05:03.267 --> 00:05:06.634
The ankle is a joint
made up of three bones --

00:05:06.634 --> 00:05:09.133
the talus, the tibia,
and the fibula.

00:05:09.133 --> 00:05:11.267
The thing is, there is a risk

00:05:11.267 --> 00:05:15.300
of being too specific
when you tell a joke.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.767
I think if you say,
you know, talus or tibia

00:05:17.767 --> 00:05:19.467
instead of ankle bone,

00:05:19.467 --> 00:05:23.734
I would worry that
I would be stealing moves

00:05:23.734 --> 00:05:27.267
from Dennis Miller,
the sort of king of specificity.

00:05:27.267 --> 00:05:29.367
I think he could
get away with that.

00:05:29.367 --> 00:05:33.667
But I want to sort of fall back
on ankle bone. You know.

00:05:37.501 --> 00:05:39.501
I don't want to be out there
being like...

00:05:39.501 --> 00:05:42.367
[As Miller] "Bought a ticket
on the Jackrabbit."

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:48.133
"From a kid with deader eyes
than Boo Radley.

00:05:48.133 --> 00:05:49.868
Looked down in the wheel well.

00:05:49.868 --> 00:05:52.100
There's a talus
banging against the tibia

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:55.534
like the ball bearings
in Captain Queeg's hand."

00:05:55.534 --> 00:05:57.267
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.367 --> 00:06:02.200
[Normal voice]
That's his.

00:06:05.067 --> 00:06:08.667
Doritos are not potato chips.

00:06:08.667 --> 00:06:10.200
They are corn chips.

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:13.634
We talked about
throwing a Dorito

00:06:13.634 --> 00:06:17.334
to a bunch of pigeons,
and that was incorrect.

00:06:17.334 --> 00:06:21.334
If you throw a potato chip to
a bunch of pigeons on a beach,

00:06:21.334 --> 00:06:23.267
as we established
in the "Closer Look,"

00:06:23.267 --> 00:06:24.834
they would be like,
"Mah-mah-mah-mah!"

00:06:24.834 --> 00:06:27.033
If it's a corn chip,
they're like, "Mah-mah--

00:06:27.033 --> 00:06:28.834
Mah! Mah! Mah!"

00:06:34.901 --> 00:06:37.868
Tampa has a great airport.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.267
Kind of joked down Tampa,

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:43.200
but I was in their airport
this summer.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:45.300
It's an outstanding airport.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:48.968
And the only thing I'd say
to the people of Tampa is, like,

00:06:48.968 --> 00:06:52.501
sometimes I just have to
sort of throw chum

00:06:52.501 --> 00:06:55.467
to the liberal elites
that watch this show, you know?

00:06:55.467 --> 00:06:57.067
[ Laughter ]

00:07:00.767 --> 00:07:03.934
I want to be a talk-show host
for all America.

00:07:06.501 --> 00:07:08.667
It's tough.

00:07:08.667 --> 00:07:11.534
Oh, we said there was a Subway
sandwich called "The Rudy"

00:07:11.534 --> 00:07:14.367
that was two pieces of bread --

00:07:14.367 --> 00:07:16.167
All it was
was two pieces of bread

00:07:16.167 --> 00:07:19.567
and a bunch of [bleep] nuts.

00:07:19.567 --> 00:07:21.868
But old Graphics was like,
"And lettuce!"

00:07:21.868 --> 00:07:23.834
[ Laughter ]

00:07:26.834 --> 00:07:29.000
"We thought the lettuce
was implied.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:32.367
Why? Did you hear
from a hundred ass [bleep]?"

00:07:32.367 --> 00:07:34.200
[ Laughter ]

00:07:40.167 --> 00:07:42.501
Also, someone said, "There are
peanuts and cashews in there.

00:07:42.501 --> 00:07:44.200
Those aren't nuts."

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:45.834
[ Sighs ]

00:07:45.834 --> 00:07:48.267
[ Chuckles ]

00:07:48.267 --> 00:07:51.367
Peanuts and cashews aren't nuts!
Ankles aren't bones!

00:07:51.367 --> 00:07:53.267
There's no such thing
as seagulls!

00:07:53.267 --> 00:07:57.367
It's fun doing a show for you!

00:07:57.367 --> 00:07:58.767
It's fun!

00:07:58.767 --> 00:08:00.334
[ Laughter ]

00:08:02.868 --> 00:08:06.234
Oh, we talked about Trump
wearing Hannibal Lecter's mask

00:08:06.234 --> 00:08:07.801
to stop him from speaking.

00:08:07.801 --> 00:08:10.667
Hannibal Lecter's mask
did not stop him from speaking.

00:08:10.667 --> 00:08:12.634
There's a whole scene
where he talks through it.

00:08:12.634 --> 00:08:15.467
It stopped him from biting.

00:08:15.467 --> 00:08:16.901
It's so --
That movie is so good.

00:08:16.901 --> 00:08:18.400
I love that movie.

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:20.334
The movie is terrifying.

00:08:20.334 --> 00:08:23.100
Wonderfully acted,
written, directed.

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:26.000
It's so funny looking back

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:29.434
that the main thing the villain
did was bite people.

00:08:29.434 --> 00:08:32.734
Like, to the degree --
Because anybody can bite.

00:08:32.734 --> 00:08:35.334
But his biting was so good,

00:08:35.334 --> 00:08:39.968
they had to take extra steps
to prevent him from biting.

00:08:39.968 --> 00:08:43.868
And even after they did that,
he still got a lot of bites in.

00:08:43.868 --> 00:08:47.267
Like, he's strapped down
like this,

00:08:47.267 --> 00:08:50.334
and they still were like,
"Let's put a thing here."

00:08:50.334 --> 00:08:51.601
All you'd have to say is, like,

00:08:51.601 --> 00:08:54.267
"Just don't get in
the bite zone."

00:08:54.267 --> 00:08:56.667
[ Laughter ]

00:08:56.667 --> 00:08:59.234
And someone was like, "I think
we just put the mask on."

00:08:59.234 --> 00:09:01.334
They were like,
"How good is he at biting?"

00:09:01.334 --> 00:09:04.901
They're like, "He's so good."

00:09:04.901 --> 00:09:08.234
So many steps so that
he wouldn't bite anybody,

00:09:08.234 --> 00:09:11.834
and everybody gets bitten!

00:09:11.834 --> 00:09:14.367
I feel like
if you were a prison guard

00:09:14.367 --> 00:09:16.200
who got bit
by Hannibal Lecter,

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:19.901
you just want him to
finish the job and eat you up.

00:09:19.901 --> 00:09:20.968
Because you'd be --

00:09:20.968 --> 00:09:22.868
If the other prison guards
saw it,

00:09:22.868 --> 00:09:24.968
you would get so much grief.

00:09:24.968 --> 00:09:26.801
They'd be like,
"Hey, Joe, uh, can't help

00:09:26.801 --> 00:09:29.801
but notice you got bite marks
on your cheek there."

00:09:29.801 --> 00:09:31.901
"Yeah, yeah, yeah, I got bit."

00:09:31.901 --> 00:09:34.200
[ Laughter ]

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:36.367
"Who was it, Joe?
Uh, which one of the prisoners?"

00:09:36.367 --> 00:09:38.167
"You [bleep] know who it was!"

00:09:38.167 --> 00:09:39.667
[ Laughter ]

00:09:42.634 --> 00:09:44.234
Um...

00:09:44.234 --> 00:09:45.634
I keep saying "uh-SIGH" berry.

00:09:45.634 --> 00:09:48.734
It's pronounced "uh-suh-ee."

00:09:48.734 --> 00:09:51.033
And to that, I say ugh.

00:09:51.033 --> 00:09:53.400
Or better yet -- ug-guh-huh.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:55.267
[ Laughter ]

00:09:57.067 --> 00:09:59.434
Um...

00:09:59.434 --> 00:10:02.100
Let's see. Uh, McDonald's.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:03.901
We made a joke about
how McDonald's

00:10:03.901 --> 00:10:05.667
shut down their ball pits

00:10:05.667 --> 00:10:08.367
because they kept finding
dead bodies in them.

00:10:08.367 --> 00:10:10.901
There is still one active
ball pit in America.

00:10:10.901 --> 00:10:15.367
It's in Marlborough, Mass.
So apologies.

00:10:15.367 --> 00:10:18.968
I guess people still go
into that ball pit every day.

00:10:18.968 --> 00:10:21.767
But here's a cool fact.
No one leaves.

00:10:21.767 --> 00:10:24.167
[ Thunder crashes ]

00:10:28.167 --> 00:10:29.634
[ Laughter ]

00:10:29.634 --> 00:10:31.901
Yeah.

00:10:31.901 --> 00:10:33.667
Sometimes you get
the camera shot just right,

00:10:33.667 --> 00:10:35.200
and it doesn't pay off.

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:37.100
[ Laughter ]

00:10:41.801 --> 00:10:43.400
We said this is the sound

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:45.667
of Wile E. Coyote
falling off a cliff,

00:10:45.667 --> 00:10:48.934
and we replaced it with
a gavel hitting the "lectern."

00:10:48.934 --> 00:10:50.667
And...

00:10:50.667 --> 00:10:52.801
[ Laughter ]

00:10:52.801 --> 00:10:54.968
But someone said,
that's not the sound

00:10:54.968 --> 00:10:56.267
of him falling off a cliff.

00:10:56.267 --> 00:10:58.334
It's the sound of him
hitting the ground.

00:10:58.334 --> 00:11:01.934
And also when the coyote
hits the ground,

00:11:01.934 --> 00:11:04.267
you wouldn't hear the sound
right away.

00:11:04.267 --> 00:11:06.868
You'd hear it
like two seconds later

00:11:06.868 --> 00:11:09.067
as the sound traveled back up.

00:11:09.067 --> 00:11:10.534
So we redid it.

00:11:10.534 --> 00:11:12.467
Here is the sound

00:11:12.467 --> 00:11:14.834
of Wile E. Coyote
hitting the ground.

00:11:14.834 --> 00:11:18.667
[ Whistle! ]

00:11:20.534 --> 00:11:21.934
-[Bleep] off!

00:11:21.934 --> 00:11:24.167
[ Laughter ]

00:11:29.501 --> 00:11:33.267
We busted Wally
in yesterday's "Closer Look"

00:11:33.267 --> 00:11:34.734
for having --

00:11:34.734 --> 00:11:37.367
He had a line
in Monday's "Closer Look."

00:11:37.367 --> 00:11:39.434
The line was, "Well, Seth..."

00:11:39.434 --> 00:11:41.000
And he thought
it was short enough

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:42.868
that he wouldn't need
one of his other guys

00:11:42.868 --> 00:11:44.267
to hold his cue cards.

00:11:44.267 --> 00:11:45.434
And then we saw in the edit

00:11:45.434 --> 00:11:47.167
that he had something
written on his hand,

00:11:47.167 --> 00:11:48.901
and we zoomed in,
it said, "Well, Seth."

00:11:48.901 --> 00:11:51.300
So, obviously --
And Wally's since explained it.

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:54.167
He just -- You know, he had some
other cues he wanted to make.

00:11:54.167 --> 00:11:55.868
He's a professional.

00:11:55.868 --> 00:11:59.434
And I didn't want to
call attention to it.

00:11:59.434 --> 00:12:02.167
It was Sal.

00:12:02.167 --> 00:12:07.767
It's so weird because no one
is more pro-labor than Sal.

00:12:07.767 --> 00:12:09.868
I mean, Sal is the most
pro-labor person I've ever met.

00:12:09.868 --> 00:12:12.501
Sal wrote an incredible piece
in "The New Republic"

00:12:12.501 --> 00:12:14.234
about the writers strike.

00:12:14.234 --> 00:12:15.601
It's really a beautiful --
no surprise --

00:12:15.601 --> 00:12:17.000
piece of writing from Sal.

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:19.033
He's got this weird blind spot

00:12:19.033 --> 00:12:22.133
about cue-card guys, though.

00:12:22.133 --> 00:12:23.434
He just, like --

00:12:23.434 --> 00:12:26.667
He treats them bad.

00:12:26.667 --> 00:12:31.434
Behind his back,
they all call him Boss Genteel.

00:12:31.434 --> 00:12:32.734
And he's always telling us,

00:12:32.734 --> 00:12:34.234
"We should do the show
without him."

00:12:34.234 --> 00:12:36.167
And I'm like, "We can't do
the show without him."

00:12:36.167 --> 00:12:38.567
He's like, "We could
if you'd memorize your lines!"

00:12:41.934 --> 00:12:44.767
"They're my words!
Don't you see?!

00:12:44.767 --> 00:12:46.934
They're just moving them
from one place to the other!

00:12:46.934 --> 00:12:50.167
But, oh, they're the heroes!"

00:12:50.167 --> 00:12:52.434
It's very ugly.
He's so mean to Wally.

00:12:52.434 --> 00:12:55.167
Wally will be like,
"How was your weekend, Sal?"

00:12:55.167 --> 00:12:57.133
He's like,
"Oh, it was wonderful, Wally.

00:12:57.133 --> 00:13:01.901
I went to the teleprompter shop!

00:13:01.901 --> 00:13:03.868
Brought my wife and my mistress!

00:13:03.868 --> 00:13:06.534
I said, 'Ladies,
you can each pick one out!'"

00:13:10.634 --> 00:13:14.234
"Your days are numbered, Wally!

00:13:14.234 --> 00:13:15.868
Oh, I can see it now!

00:13:15.868 --> 00:13:17.534
'Here lies Cue Card Wally.

00:13:17.534 --> 00:13:20.100
Cause of death --
march of time.'"

00:13:20.100 --> 00:13:22.033
[ Laughter ]

00:13:27.167 --> 00:13:30.467
I mentioned the chemical
in thermal receipts.

00:13:30.467 --> 00:13:32.000
I was told
it should be pronounced

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:33.801
the way you say "biscuit."

00:13:33.801 --> 00:13:36.634
So I said "bye-sphenol."

00:13:36.634 --> 00:13:39.434
But I should have said
"biscuit."

00:13:39.434 --> 00:13:41.067
[ Laughter ]

00:13:47.567 --> 00:13:50.200
I said I didn't know
football games had ushers

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:53.033
because I get taken straight
to a luxury box.

00:13:53.033 --> 00:13:54.868
Someone said,
"Who takes you if not an usher?"

00:13:54.868 --> 00:13:56.534
Well, my personal manservant.

00:13:56.534 --> 00:13:58.567
[ Laughter ]

00:14:00.601 --> 00:14:05.567
I'm not gonna let a stranger
take me to a box.

00:14:05.567 --> 00:14:07.300
Kidnapped much?

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:08.968
[ Laughter ]

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:15.334
Here's a question.
We've dealt with this before.

00:14:15.334 --> 00:14:17.367
Is the Speaker of the House
second in line

00:14:17.367 --> 00:14:19.133
to the presidency
or are they third in line?

00:14:19.133 --> 00:14:20.567
It goes
President, Vice President,

00:14:20.567 --> 00:14:21.834
Speaker of the House.

00:14:21.834 --> 00:14:23.701
We want to clarify.
We looked.

00:14:23.701 --> 00:14:26.167
So, we actually looked
in the Constitution,

00:14:26.167 --> 00:14:28.033
and it says there --
and I quote --

00:14:28.033 --> 00:14:30.334
"It's whatever one
you want it to be."

00:14:30.334 --> 00:14:32.100
[ Laughter ]

00:14:33.767 --> 00:14:36.734
Here's a comment we got
this week.

00:14:36.734 --> 00:14:38.400
This is in the comments section.

00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:40.501
Someone decided, "Oh."
Watching it, and they're like,

00:14:40.501 --> 00:14:42.133
"Oh, I'll make sure
I write this down.

00:14:42.133 --> 00:14:45.100
Want to make sure they see it."

00:14:47.734 --> 00:14:50.434
"What the [bleep]
is this boring, stupid show?"

00:14:50.434 --> 00:14:52.000
[ Laughter ]

00:14:54.868 --> 00:14:56.801
That's a good question.
Here's one for you.

00:14:56.801 --> 00:14:59.767
Why the [bleep]
are you watching it?

00:14:59.767 --> 00:15:01.868
Like, what are you doing?

00:15:01.868 --> 00:15:04.501
Like, we all know what this is.

00:15:04.501 --> 00:15:07.100
Alright?
The Jackals know what it is.

00:15:07.100 --> 00:15:08.133
I know what it is.

00:15:08.133 --> 00:15:09.834
We like this little thing
we have.

00:15:09.834 --> 00:15:12.834
You don't got to watch it, man.

00:15:12.834 --> 00:15:16.400
Why did the YouTube algorithm
even show it to you?

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:17.968
Did you watch another video

00:15:17.968 --> 00:15:21.701
where a guy made, like, dog toys
with human heads hump?

00:15:23.601 --> 00:15:25.567
You got to walk in and be like,
"What the [bleep]?"

00:15:25.567 --> 00:15:27.467
You're like somebody
who goes to a Renaissance fair

00:15:27.467 --> 00:15:30.734
and you're like, "Do you guys
not know what year it is?!"

00:15:30.734 --> 00:15:34.167
"We're having fun, dude!

00:15:34.167 --> 00:15:36.133
Eat your turkey leg

00:15:36.133 --> 00:15:38.534
and drink your [bleep] mead
out of a Solo cup

00:15:38.534 --> 00:15:41.968
or get the [bleep] out of here!"

00:15:41.968 --> 00:15:43.467
[Bleep]

00:15:43.467 --> 00:15:45.834
"Doth that make sense?"

00:15:45.834 --> 00:15:47.300
[ Laughter ]

00:15:50.868 --> 00:15:52.767
"What the [bleep] is this?"

00:15:52.767 --> 00:15:54.801
[ Laughter ]

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:01.868
We had a --
We had a joke a woman --

00:16:01.868 --> 00:16:04.100
The story was that
a woman in Australia

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:06.334
is recovering after she tried
to rescue a platypus

00:16:06.334 --> 00:16:09.734
with her bare hands
and was stabbed...

00:16:09.734 --> 00:16:12.834
with its poisonous spurs.

00:16:12.834 --> 00:16:15.300
It's not poison. It's venom.

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:17.901
Venom is injected.

00:16:17.901 --> 00:16:20.634
Poison is ingested.

00:16:20.634 --> 00:16:22.267
Now we know.

00:16:22.267 --> 00:16:25.334
Then I went off script...

00:16:25.334 --> 00:16:27.300
which I'm allowed to do.

00:16:30.033 --> 00:16:32.067
And I mimed
'cause I know a little --

00:16:32.067 --> 00:16:34.901
I know one or two things
about platypuses,

00:16:34.901 --> 00:16:37.567
that they also lay eggs,
so I mimed it laying an egg.

00:16:37.567 --> 00:16:40.701
So it turns out a lot of you
know like 300 to 400 things

00:16:40.701 --> 00:16:43.701
about platypuses...

00:16:43.701 --> 00:16:46.934
and said, "Only the male
has the venom-delivering spur,

00:16:46.934 --> 00:16:49.634
so it couldn't lay an egg."

00:16:49.634 --> 00:16:51.167
So many of you said that.

00:16:51.167 --> 00:16:54.667
I'm assuming
all Australian viewers.

00:16:54.667 --> 00:16:55.901
So I'd just like to say...

00:16:55.901 --> 00:16:57.501
[Australian accent]
I'm sorry.

00:16:57.501 --> 00:16:59.000
[ Laughter ]

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:00.701
I apologize.

00:17:00.701 --> 00:17:02.334
[ Laughter ]

00:17:05.934 --> 00:17:08.801
I feel as though I've done you
a grave injustice.

00:17:08.801 --> 00:17:10.834
[ Laughter ]

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:17.100
[Normal voice] Oh.
This has been "Animal Flubs."

00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:19.868
-♪ Animal Flubs, Animal Flubs ♪

00:17:19.868 --> 00:17:22.667
♪ It's time to take a look
at some Animal Flubs ♪

00:17:22.667 --> 00:17:25.601
♪ From the birds to the bees
to the baby bear cubs ♪

00:17:25.601 --> 00:17:27.167
♪ It's time for Animal ♪

00:17:27.167 --> 00:17:29.934
-♪ What am I? ♪

00:17:29.934 --> 00:17:33.367
♪ How am I even a thing? ♪

00:17:33.367 --> 00:17:38.133
♪ It's so weird I exist ♪

00:17:38.133 --> 00:17:41.634
♪ Do I serve any purpose? ♪

00:17:41.634 --> 00:17:46.701
♪ Do you know
how most platypuses die? ♪

00:17:46.701 --> 00:17:52.400
♪ It's when
they first see a mirror ♪

00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:56.067
♪ And they're so bummed out ♪

00:17:56.067 --> 00:18:01.200
♪ That they eat
their own venom ♪

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:03.801
♪ At which point ♪

00:18:03.801 --> 00:18:08.167
♪ The venom becomes poison ♪

00:18:08.167 --> 00:18:13.734
♪ Because it's ingested ♪

00:18:15.534 --> 00:18:17.367
Back to you, Koala.

00:18:21.033 --> 00:18:22.901
-The [bleep] was that?

00:18:27.234 --> 00:18:29.801
-What the [bleep]
is this boring, stupid show?

00:18:29.801 --> 00:18:31.300
[ Laughter ]

00:18:33.868 --> 00:18:36.767
Stevie Nicks
doesn't wear scarves.

00:18:36.767 --> 00:18:38.501
She wears shawls.

00:18:40.334 --> 00:18:43.400
So at least we finally
got to the bottom

00:18:43.400 --> 00:18:45.701
of why those jokes
haven't been landing.

00:18:45.701 --> 00:18:47.267
[ Laughter ]

00:18:50.167 --> 00:18:52.534
A lot of people said the real
Scarf King would be --

00:18:52.534 --> 00:18:55.200
Here were some of the choices.
Lenny Kravitz.

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:59.167
Little Steven
from the E Street Band.

00:18:59.167 --> 00:19:04.200
Steven Tyler
got the most answers.

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:05.667
Uh, true story --

00:19:05.667 --> 00:19:07.667
Steven Tyler's dad

00:19:07.667 --> 00:19:11.901
was Shoemaker's music teacher
in high school.

00:19:11.901 --> 00:19:14.167
And if you don't think
Shoemaker brings that up

00:19:14.167 --> 00:19:18.434
every time
an Aerosmith song plays...

00:19:18.434 --> 00:19:19.834
dream on.

00:19:19.834 --> 00:19:21.501
[ Laughter ]

00:19:26.300 --> 00:19:28.067
Let's see.

00:19:28.067 --> 00:19:29.534
[ Muttering ]

00:19:32.868 --> 00:19:34.300
[ Laughter ]

00:19:43.300 --> 00:19:44.968
Steven next week.

